---
// Figure: four measured incidents as INFO's counters show them.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
import Readout from '../shared/Readout.astro';
import './operating.css';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="op-incidents" title="What INFO shows during four incidents" controls="none"
  caption="Measured on Redis 8.10.3 on a laptop (macOS, libc malloc), not simulated. A paced cache-aside client sent 1,000 GETs a second over 50,000 keys with skewed popularity (Zipf, exponent 1), storing each miss as a 400-byte value with a TTL between 60 and 180 seconds, under maxmemory 64 MB and allkeys-lru. INFO and DBSIZE were read every second, and each recording's incident happened at 240 s. Each incident is a separate recording that starts with an empty cache, which is why the since-start ratio sits below the 10-second one, and the four steady states before 240 s differ slightly. Hit ratios and rates are computed from INFO's cumulative counters over a 10-second window, as a monitoring system would, so a burst is drawn spread over 10 seconds: the 6 MB recording evicted about 10,000 keys within two seconds, not 1,200 a second for ten. How many keys fit in 6 MB depends on the allocator.">
  <Choice slot="params" name="incident" label="Incident at 240 s" value="small"
    options={[
      { value: 'small', label: 'maxmemory cut to 6 MB' },
      { value: 'ttl', label: 'TTL cut to 10 s' },
      { value: 'rename', label: 'key names changed' },
      { value: 'flush', label: 'FLUSHALL' },
    ]} />
  <Fragment slot="stats">
    <Readout name="before" label="Hit ratio before" kind="hit" />
    <Readout name="recent" label="Last 10 s, at 420 s" kind="hit" />
    <Readout name="since" label="Since start, at 420 s" kind="neutral" />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="op-charts">
    <div data-chart="ratio"></div>
    <div data-chart="rates"></div>
    <div data-chart="keys"></div>
  </div>
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>Three charts share a time axis from 150 to 420 seconds of each recording, with the incident at 240 s: the hit ratio over the last 10 seconds and since the server started, the misses, evictions and expirations a second, and the number of keys. Before every incident the hit ratio over the last 10 seconds is about 85%, the cache holds about 19,000 to 20,000 keys, about 150 reads a second miss, there are no evictions, and between 50 and 250 keys expire a second.</p>
    <p>maxmemory cut to 6 MB: about 10,000 keys are evicted within two seconds and the cache settles at about 9,300 keys. From then on about 200 keys are evicted every second, misses rise to about 220 a second, and the hit ratio over the last 10 seconds settles at about 78%. Three minutes later the hit ratio since start has moved only from 82.7% to 80.7%.</p>
    <p>TTL cut to 10 s: nothing happens at first, because keys already stored keep their old TTLs. Over the next three minutes the old keys expire and their replacements expire quickly, so expirations stay at 250 to 480 a second, the number of keys falls steadily to about 3,800, misses rise to about 350 a second and the hit ratio over the last 10 seconds falls to about 65%, still falling at the end. There are no evictions. The hit ratio since start falls only to 78%.</p>
    <p>Key names changed: every read now misses its new name, so misses jump to almost 400 a second and the hit ratio over the last 10 seconds falls to about 62% within ten seconds, then recovers to 85% in about a minute. The old keys stay in memory until their TTLs end, so the number of keys rises to almost 26,000 before falling back. There are no evictions.</p>
    <p>FLUSHALL: the hit ratio and the misses follow almost exactly the same path as the change of key names, but the number of keys falls to almost nothing and climbs back to about 20,000 over two minutes. There are no evictions, and expirations stop for a minute because no key is old enough to expire. In all four, the hit ratio since start moves by less than five points.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { bindParams, setReadouts } from '../shared/player.mjs';
  import { lineChart } from '../shared/chart.mjs';
  import { series, at, INCIDENT } from './incidents-model.mjs';

  const pct = (v: number) => `${Math.round(v * 100)}%`;
  const n = (v: number) => Math.round(v).toLocaleString('en-GB');
  // Pad tick labels to one width so the three charts' plot areas line up.
  const pad = (f: (v: number) => string) => (v: number) => f(v).padStart(6, '\u2007');
  const x = { label: 'Seconds into the recording, from 150 s', domain: [150, 420], tickStep: 60 };
  const markers = [{ id: 'incident', x: INCIDENT, label: 'Incident', kind: 'error' }];
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="op-incidents"]').forEach(root => {
    const el = (name: string) => root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-chart="${name}"]`)!;
    const ratio = lineChart(el('ratio'), {
      label: 'Hit ratio over the last 10 seconds and since the server started',
      height: 190, x, markers,
      y: { label: 'Hit ratio', domain: [0.5, 1], tickStep: 0.1, format: pad(pct) },
      series: [
        { id: 'recent', label: 'Last 10 seconds', kind: 'hit', dash: '' },
        { id: 'sinceStart', label: 'Since start', kind: 'neutral', dash: '6 4' },
      ],
    });
    const rates = lineChart(el('rates'), {
      label: 'Misses, evictions and expirations a second, averaged over 10 seconds',
      height: 190, x, markers,
      y: { label: 'Misses, evictions and expirations a second', domain: [0, 1200], tickStep: 300, format: pad(n) },
      series: [
        { id: 'misses', label: 'Misses', kind: 'miss', dash: '' },
        { id: 'evictions', label: 'Evictions', kind: 'error', dash: '6 4' },
        { id: 'expirations', label: 'Expirations', kind: 'expiry', dash: '2 3' },
      ],
    });
    const keys = lineChart(el('keys'), {
      label: 'Number of keys in Redis',
      height: 170, x, markers,
      y: { label: 'Keys in Redis', domain: [0, 30000], tickStep: 10000, format: pad(n) },
      series: [{ id: 'keys', label: 'Keys', kind: 'redis' }],
    });
    bindParams(root, params => {
      const s = series(String(params.incident));
      ratio.set('recent', s.recent);
      ratio.set('sinceStart', s.sinceStart);
      rates.set('misses', s.misses);
      rates.set('evictions', s.evictions);
      rates.set('expirations', s.expirations);
      keys.set('keys', s.keys);
      ratio.render(); rates.render(); keys.render();
      setReadouts(root, {
        before: pct(at(s.recent, INCIDENT - 1)!),
        recent: pct(at(s.recent, 420)!),
        since: pct(at(s.sinceStart, 420)!),
      });
    });
  });
</script>
